<p>Hondarribia is considerably smaller and quieter than San Sebastián or Bilbao, which is part of its appeal but also something worth planning around on departure day. Shops, bars, and pintxo spots in the old town and La Marina tend to wind down earlier than their equivalents in a bigger city, so an early check-out or a very early flight rarely finds much open beyond a hotel breakfast, and it's worth planning a final meal or coffee stop with that smaller-town rhythm in mind rather than assuming late-night or pre-dawn options will be plentiful. There's no need to arrange parking or return a rental car before an early departure, since a private driver collects you directly from your hotel or address at whatever hour your flight requires.</p>
